From 75d8a4e021a23b6352a74d9786c9b89e6ed731f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 23:47:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] [feature](be) Add snapshot remote unwind accessors
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements the unw_accessors_t callbacks the HTTP coordinator hands to
unw_create_addr_space + unw_init_remote so libunwind walks frames out
of the in-memory snapshot (ucontext_t + 8 KiB stack slice) captured by
the worker signal handler. Mirrors obstack-master's shape (ptrace
_UPT_accessors → in-memory accessors) so the unwind half of this
variant is auditable against an existing libunwind remote consumer.

Key accessors:
- access_mem prefers the captured stack slice for stack-pointer reads;
  falls through to live process memory for readable mappings (DWARF
  tables, GOT). Returns -UNW_EINVAL outside both so the unwind
  terminates rather than wandering into unmapped memory.
- access_reg maps libunwind's UNW_X86_64_* reg numbers onto glibc's
  ucontext_t gregs[] indices; x86_64 only (early-return -UNW_EBADREG
  on other arches, mirroring the snapshot handler).
- find_proc_info / put_unwind_info / get_dyn_info_list_addr delegate to
  libunwind's local accessors so the binary's .eh_frame is the source of
  truth for proc info. Safe because the coordinator runs on the HTTP
  action thread, not in a signal handler.

UNW_CACHE_GLOBAL matches obstack since .eh_frame is process-wide.

Reference: <obstack>/src/main.cpp:354-363,413-423
Reference: libunwind-common.h:191-211 (unw_accessors_t shape)
Reference: libunwind-x86_64.h:58-74 (UNW_X86_64_* register enum)
---
 be/src/common/srunwind_remote_unwind.cpp | 308 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 be/src/common/srunwind_remote_unwind.h   |  73 ++++++
 2 files changed, 381 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 be/src/common/srunwind_remote_unwind.cpp
 create mode 100644 be/src/common/srunwind_remote_unwind.h

